From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:32:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): all six cursor shapes, exactly

DoubleUnderscore and Vintage were both being sent as a plain underline. I called
that an approximation; it was a different shape, and it looked like one - a
stacked pair and a fat bottom bar are not underlines.

ghostty patch 31 adds both, so all six of WT's shapes now map exactly and
nothing is being rounded off. cursorHeight is still not forwarded: it exists to
size Vintage, and underline_thick is a fixed quarter of the cell, which is what
WT itself defaults cursorHeight to - sending a height would imply an effect
ghostty has no setting for.

WT suites: terminalCore 54/54, unitSettingsModel 159/159, unitControl 62/62,
terminalApp 51/51.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 .../GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp             | 21 +++++++++++++------
 .../GhosttySettingsTests.cpp                  | 12 +++++------
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
index 4d04dfe8b..614ab7d8b 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
@@ -111,11 +111,16 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // beside it drew a bar, because the profile's cursorShape was never
         // forwarded and ghostty used its own default.
         //
-        // ghostty offers four shapes to WT's six. DoubleUnderscore and Vintage
-        // both become an underline - Vintage is a short underscore and ghostty
-        // has no height control for it, which is also why CursorHeight is not
-        // forwarded at all. Those two are the approximations; the other four
-        // are exact.
+        // All six shapes map exactly. ghostty had four until patch 31 added the
+        // two DECSCUSR has no name for - a stacked double underline and the
+        // thick bottom bar the Windows console has drawn for decades. They were
+        // both collapsed onto a plain underline before that, which was not an
+        // approximation so much as a different shape.
+        //
+        // CursorHeight is still not forwarded: it exists to size Vintage, and
+        // cursor-style underline_thick is a fixed quarter of the cell - which is
+        // what WT itself defaults cursorHeight to. Sending a height would imply
+        // an effect ghostty has no setting for.
         //
         // Only the default is set here. A program can still ask for a different
         // shape with DECSCUSR, on either engine, and ghostty's shell
@@ -129,9 +134,13 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
                 set("cursor-style", "bar");
                 break;
             case Core::CursorStyle::Underscore:
+                set("cursor-style", "underline");
+                break;
             case Core::CursorStyle::DoubleUnderscore:
+                set("cursor-style", "underline_double");
+                break;
             case Core::CursorStyle::Vintage:
-                set("cursor-style", "underline");
+                set("cursor-style", "underline_thick");
                 break;
             case Core::CursorStyle::EmptyBox:
                 set("cursor-style", "block_hollow");
diff --git a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
index 73ad2b208..d2de9437d 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/UnitTests_Control/GhosttySettingsTests.cpp
@@ -187,9 +187,10 @@ namespace ControlUnitTests
     // Found by hand: a ghostty pane drew a block cursor beside a cascadia pane
     // drawing a bar, because the profile's cursorShape was never forwarded.
     //
-    // ghostty has four shapes to WT's six. Vintage and DoubleUnderscore both
-    // land on underline - those two are approximations and the mapping should
-    // say so out loud rather than be discovered later.
+    // All six map exactly. ghostty had four until patch 31 added the two
+    // DECSCUSR has no name for; before that these last two were collapsed onto
+    // a plain underline, which was not an approximation so much as a different
+    // shape, and it looked like it.
     void GhosttySettingsTests::CursorShapeIsForwarded()
     {
         struct Case
@@ -202,9 +203,8 @@ namespace ControlUnitTests
             { Core::CursorStyle::FilledBox, "block" },
             { Core::CursorStyle::EmptyBox, "block_hollow" },
             { Core::CursorStyle::Underscore, "underline" },
-            // Approximations: ghostty has neither.
-            { Core::CursorStyle::DoubleUnderscore, "underline" },
-            { Core::CursorStyle::Vintage, "underline" },
+            { Core::CursorStyle::DoubleUnderscore, "underline_double" },
+            { Core::CursorStyle::Vintage, "underline_thick" },
         };
 
         for (const auto& c : cases)
